ble, your own policy usually responds to both units, with a tenant’s renters policy covering their belongings. Check your policy and keep separate records for each unit."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are ice dams covered in Cuyahoga County homeowners policies?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Many policies cover interior water damage caused by ice dams, while excluding the cost of the ice itself or general roof wear. Disputes are usually about how far the damage extends into insulation, walls and roof decking."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Why did the insurer pay so little for the plaster in my Lakewood home?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Estimates often price plaster ceilings and walls as standard drywall. If your home has lath and plaster, an appraiser can document the material and the extra labor involved so the scope matches what was actually damaged."}}],"@id":"https://ohioinsuranceappraiser.com/service-cities/cleveland-ohio/#faq"},{"@type":"Service","name":"Insurance appraisal in Cleveland, Ohio","serviceType":"Insurance appraisal","description":"Cleveland, Ohio insurance appraiser for ice dam, burst pipe and windstorm claims on century homes and doubles across Cuyahoga County and the lake.","provider":{"@id":"https://ohioinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"areaServed":{"@type":"City","name":"Cleveland","containedInPlace":{"@type":"State","name":"Ohio"}},"url":"https://ohioinsuranceappraiser.com/service-cities/cleveland-ohio/","@id":"https://ohioinsuranceappraiser.com/service-cities/cleveland-ohio/#service"}]}</script>
